---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import PageCoda from '../components/PageCoda.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Artwork from '../components/Artwork.astro';
import { breadcrumbs, founderPage } from '../lib/seo';

// The page that says who runs the site (docs/seo-aeo-plan.md §8 S1): the
// founder block below is the ProfilePage's main entity, and every chapter's
// author Person links here. The date is the block's last real change.
const jsonLd = [
  breadcrumbs([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]),
  founderPage('2026-10-16'),
];
---

<Base
  title="About AgentRiders — the guild for people who run AI agents"
  description="Everyone is building dragons. We are here for the people who ride them."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="About" title="Why riders." description="Everyone is building dragons. We are here for the people who ride them." art="eye" id="about-title"></PageHero>

  <section class="section section--bone">
    <div class="container inner-art-layout">
      <div class="prose manifesto-prose">
        <p>An agent can do a week of work in an afternoon. It can also spend $400 in tokens doing the wrong thing, confidently. Both are true at once, and that is what makes it a dragon: powerful, willful, and full of its own ideas about what you meant.</p>
        <p>The dragons improve every quarter without your help. What does not improve on its own is the riding: the scoping, the budgets, the judgment about when to hold on and when to let go. The human is the bottleneck. That also makes the human the hero — the riding is where all the leverage is.</p>
        <p>Autonomy is earned, not granted. Every agent gets a scope, a budget and a kill switch before its first flight, and looser reins only after it lands a few. Nobody here hands a hatchling the production keys and calls it trust.</p>
        <p>Logs beat opinions. Opinions about agents are cheap and mostly wrong; a record of what ran, what it cost and what burned is neither. We keep the numbers in because that is the only way anyone learns anything.</p>
        <p>The Guild exists so nobody has to learn every lesson alone, at their own expense. Somebody here has already been burned the way you are about to be. Read their log. Then fly, and log yours.</p>
        <h2 id="author">Who runs it</h2>
        <p><strong>Max Faingezicht</strong> is the founder of AgentRiders and of Permanent Ventures Inc. He builds the site by running agents on real work and logging the flights: the <a href="/logs/shipped-agentriders-phase-2/">log of the flight that shipped the site</a> is public, and so is his <a href="/riders/maxcr/">rider profile</a>. Find him on <a href="https://github.com/maxfain" rel="me">GitHub</a>, or write to <a href="mailto:hello@agentriders.com">hello@agentriders.com</a>.</p>
        <h2 id="how-this-site-is-made">How this site is made</h2>
        <p>The chapters and lessons are written by the founder. Agents are used to build the site and to draft; every number in a flight log comes from the rider who flew it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="manifesto-art"><figure class="inner-art"><Artwork name="bond" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 45vw, 100vw" alt="A rider and a copper dragon build trust, face to face." /><figcaption class="micro">THE HUMAN IS THE HERO.</figcaption></figure><p class="manifesto-quote">The dragons get better.<br /><em>So should the riders.</em></p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <PageCoda />
</Base>
